# NCC: Pre-update hard gate

## You (and agents) before `ncc system-update`

Run and get **exit 0**:

```bash
bash tests/validate-ncc-nix.sh
```

Still small (~seconds). **Do this before every local/remote update** that deploys `nixos/` changes. Do not skip “because it’s only a small edit.”

**Forbidden:** telling the user to `ncc system-update` / claiming “validated” if this did not exit 0 **in this turn**.

## What it already auto-detects

| Check | Catches |
|-------|---------|
| bash-in-nix | `${…}` footguns in `''` strings across `nixos/` |
| packages/lib layer | relative imports into foreign `packages/lib` |
| module layer | install-wizard paths in system-update/plans; cross-module imports under `nixos/modules/` |
| **migrations auto-detect** | packaging-sensitive deletes without `<module>/migrations/`; version `< migration to`; `isDataNix` orphans without migration |
| install-wizard packaging | same path as system-update `scriptTree` |

Version bump is **only required when that gate (or a broken rebuild) says so** — see `ncc-module-migrations.mdc`. Not every file edit needs a bump.

## Optional extras (not a substitute)

```bash
bash tests/install-wizard/validate-no-hardcoded-paths.sh
bash tests/gui/validate-gui-python.sh   # if GUI touched
```

`nix-instantiate --parse` on one file is **never** enough.
